# One live site

The published site is GitHub `master` at https://pattyong8.github.io. There is one repo: `pattyong8/pattyong8.github.io`.

## Before any edit

1. `git fetch origin` and work on the latest `origin/master`.
2. If HEAD is not `master`, switch to `master` and fast-forward. Do not keep live-site work only on `redesign/scrapbook` or a `cursor/*` agent branch.
3. Only create a side branch when the user explicitly asks for one, and say that it will not go live until it is merged into `master`.

## Publishing

- GitHub Pages publishes `master`. Pushing `redesign/scrapbook` does not update the phone site.
- Never commit Finder duplicates (`* 2.jpeg`, `* 2.css`), `_incoming/`, `.DS_Store`, or `travel-page-tool/.batch-2026-results.json`.
- After a publish, stay on `master`.

## If desktop and phone disagree

The Mac copy drifted from live. Pull `origin/master` first, then re-apply only the missing Mac change on top. Do not treat `redesign/scrapbook` as current.
